.TH CTPOOL_FUTURE_FULFILL 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ctpool_future_fulfill \- deliver a result to a detached future
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadpool.h>

ccol_retval_t ctpool_future_fulfill(ctpool_future *f, void *result);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Delivers result to a future created via ctpool_future_create_detached,
waking any callers currently blocked in ctpool_future_get, then
releases the producer's reference (freeing the future here if the
caller already released its own reference via ctpool_future_free).

Must be called exactly once per detached future. Do not call this on
a future returned by ctpool_submit_future, ctpool_try_submit_future,
or ctpool_timed_submit_future; those are fulfilled internally by the
worker thread that runs their task.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
f        Future handle; must have been created via
         ctpool_future_create_detached and not already fulfilled
result   Result value to deliver; retrievable via ctpool_future_get
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        result was delivered
ccol_invalid_args   f is NULL
ccol_not_permitted  f was already fulfilled
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_future_create_detached (3),
.BR ctpool_future_get (3),
.BR ctpool_future_done (3),
.BR ctpool_future_free (3)
